WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:02.420
Speaker 1: very interesting news.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:08.450
Even though Joe Biden has not said he wants
to increase the number of justices on the

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:14.210
Supreme Court and is awaiting a report about
the Supreme Court, Democrats in the House

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:19.350
and Senate will be introducing legislation
that would do exactly that.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.330
It would expand the number of seats on the
court from nine to 13.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.730
Many progressive groups like it.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:34.170
This is being led by Congressman Jerry Nadler,
Hank Johnson, Monder Jones.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:39.460
And in the Senate, Senator Ed Markey likes
this same idea.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.110
It is way too early to know whether this has
a shot in in the house.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:49.240
I think, listen, without Joe Biden clearly
saying, let's do this, I don't think there's

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.380
any way in hell that it passes the Senate.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:55.809
But it is a very interesting step that is
going to be taken.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:01:00.120
I've said before, I'm open.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:08.790
My general view is I am not that into ideas
that can be turned against those who implement

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.950
them, and I've said, you know, if you increase
from nine to 13, then the next time Republicans

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.580
have control, they could go from 13 to 17.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.750
And that becomes sort of like a race to the
bottom.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.610
And that doesn't seem great.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:25.990
We have a unique situation, though, where
Republicans, to their credit, I mean, listen,

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:32.300
they pulled it off, but disgustingly argued
we don't put in new Supreme Court justices

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.400
during the last year of a presidential term
when Barack Obama nominated Merrick Garland.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:43.970
And then with just weeks to go before an election
in twenty twenty, they pushed through the

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:51.960
Amy Amy CONI or Amy covid Barrett nomination
for Donald Trump to replace Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:59.200
That, to me, passes a line where I believe
a threshold has been met for more sort of

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.890
aggressive action being needed.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:06.430
So like I would be OK with expanding the court,
I would be worried about what the long term

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.850
impact would be.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:14.310
We definitely need to be looking at term limits
on Supreme Court justices so that it's simply

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:15.310
predetermined.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.560
You know, I don't know exactly how the numbers
would work out, but with nine justices on

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.340
the court, that means that there is one.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.750
And with, you know, imagine it's nine justices,
18 year terms.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.920
That means every six years there is a retirement
and a replacement and, you know, ahead of

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.860
time what the schedule of that is, whatever
the numbers would actually work out to.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.390
I believe that that's something that would
be important to do.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.020
And I very much support that now this bill.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.290
When is Joe Biden going to take a position
on it?

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:52.960
My thought from the beginning was Joe Biden
is deliberately not taking a position in the

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.320
lead up to the election because it could be
misused one way or the other.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.090
It's unclear what the benefit would be.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.140
We were told Joe Biden would have a group
give him recommendations about what to do

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.980
with the Supreme Court.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.000
Last week, we learned now the group's not
actually going to give recommendations.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.080
It's just going to be a report about the state
of the judiciary and the court.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.430
So then the question is, well, who is going
to give Joe Biden recommendations as to what

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.770
to do and when is he going to get those recommendations?

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:21.350
The way I see it right now is relatively cynical.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.150
And it's this is going to be a punt.

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.040
And you're not going to hear I mean, he just
he won't expand the court.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.040
He won't necessarily say I am committed never
to expanding the court.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.640
He will just say at this time, I am not expanding
the court.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.290
I'm not moving to expand the court.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.690
And that that will go on and on.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.170
That's my view.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.230
If you think it'll go a different way.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.230
Let me know.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.560
You can find me on Twitter at the Pakman.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.370
We have a fantastic show for you today.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:04:09.860
This will be the best Friday show in at least

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:18.450
a week.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.300
All right.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.830
Stay with us.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:33.820
We'll be 

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:48.520
right back.

